  "id": "BIT-phpmyadmin-2026-119561",
  "summary": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 WebAuthn Two-Factor Authentication Bypass via CustomServer",
  "details": "phpMyAdmin through 5.2.3 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability in CustomServer::parseAndValidateAssertionResponse() that never verifies WebAuthn assertion signatures against stored public keys. Attackers holding a victim's MySQL credentials can POST a crafted webauthn_request_response with matching challenge, origin, and rpIdHash to bypass the second factor and gain database privileges.",
